Spec: Commerce taxonomy and merchandising — Phase C
Platform: Loadder canonical Commerce + Store Studio V16
Purpose:
  Replace legacy product category/brand text as the source of truth with
  workspace-scoped canonical taxonomy, and provide truthful merchandising
  sources to the existing V16 product presentation.
Owns:
  - Canonical Commerce Categories, Brands, Collections and collection membership.
  - Product assignment to canonical taxonomy records.
  - Product-section source resolution for Featured, Newest, On-sale and manual
    Collections in Store Studio V16.
Can modify:
  - server/db/migrations/094_commerce_taxonomy_merchandising.mjs
  - server/app/services/ecommerce-service.mjs
  - server/app/routes/ecommerce.mjs
  - src/pages/StoreCommerceManagerPageCore.tsx
  - src/components/store-studio-v16/
  - focused Commerce/V16 tests and isolated E2E.
Must:
  - Scope every taxonomy and merchandising record, lookup and mutation to the
    authenticated workspace and to its owning STORE Site Project where relevant.
  - Give Categories and Brands stable IDs and workspace-unique slugs, with
    active/archive lifecycle. Archived records remain readable for existing
    products but cannot be newly assigned.
  - Backfill nonblank legacy ecommerce_products.category and .brand values
    idempotently into canonical records, preserving product ownership and never
    creating a record for blank or whitespace-only values.
  - Make product category_id and brand_id the canonical source after backfill;
    legacy text is compatibility display data only.
  - Support manual Collections and ordered membership, plus deterministic
    Featured, Newest and On-sale sources from canonical product data.
  - Defer Best sellers: it is unavailable unless a reliable eligible-order
    evidence contract exists. No fabricated sales ranking.
  - Extend the existing V16 product section and renderer only; preserve manual
    Product Slots and do not introduce a renderer or Website product copies.
  - Keep selected variant/cart/checkout/order truth in canonical Commerce.
  - Keep the management UX usable in RTL at 390px.
Must not:
  - Copy Products, Variants, Inventory, Cart, Orders or Payments into Website
    records or published snapshots.
  - Create Store Studio V17, a parallel Commerce runtime, or an invented
    best-seller signal.
  - Modify protected visual-checkout baseline 82217cc.
Done when:
  - Focused migration, service, route and V16 regressions prove lifecycle,
    legacy backfill, isolation, collision safety, source selection and Store
    compatibility; isolated browser flows prove management and 390px behavior.
Scenario: Idempotent legacy transition
  Given products in one workspace with legacy nonblank category and brand text
  When the taxonomy migration runs more than once
  Then each normalized value has one canonical record in that workspace
  And products retain stable canonical assignments
  And blank values create no taxonomy records.
Scenario: Truthful merchandising
  Given a Store Studio V16 product section
  When a merchant chooses Featured, Newest, On-sale or a manual Collection
  Then the renderer resolves products from canonical Commerce only
  And draft Website content contains only the chosen source reference
  And Best sellers is not offered without eligible-order evidence.
